---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import DanaNote from '../components/DanaNote.astro';
import NightAtlas from '../components/NightAtlas.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Night - Svapna Project"
  description="One night of sleep, hour by hour: what the Upaniṣads, the Tibetan yogas, the Sufis, the Daoists and the sleep laboratory each find in waking, dreaming, deep sleep and lucidity."
>
  <section>
    <SectionHeader
      num="Annex"
      kicker="A night, hour by hour"
      title="The Night"
      sub="One night of sleep, from lying down to morning. At each depth: what the traditions and the laboratory found there."
    />
    <NightAtlas />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 hairline-b hairline-t">
      <div class="md:col-span-2 p-5 md:p-8 hairline-b md:hairline-r md:border-b-0">
        <span class="mono text-[9px] md:text-[10px] uppercase tracking-widest text-neutral-500">On the chart</span>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-10 p-6 sm:p-8 md:p-12 max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-base leading-loose text-neutral-700">
          The line is a hypnogram: the shape of an ordinary night as a sleep laboratory records it, idealised. Deep sleep gathers early; the dreaming periods lengthen towards morning. The ten stations and the voices set along it come from the <a href="/library" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:italic">Library</a>’s quote bank, the <a href="/history" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:italic">History</a> timeline and the <a href="/curriculum" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:italic">Curriculum</a>. The pairing of a tradition’s term with an hour of the night is an editorial reading, not a claim that the traditions describe the same thing. Not medical advice: <a href="/about/disclaimer" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:italic">disclaimer</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <DanaNote />
  </section>
</Layout>
